    "solution": "class Solution:\r\n    def sortArray(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[int]:\r\n        def merge(arr, L, M, R):\r\n            left, right = arr[L:M+1], arr[M+1:R+1]\r\n            i, j, k = L, 0, 0\r\n            while j < len(left) and k < len(right):\r\n                if left[j] <= right[k]:\r\n                    arr[i] = left[j]\r\n                    j += 1\r\n                else:\r\n                    arr[i] = right[k]\r\n                    k += 1\r\n                i += 1\r\n            while j < len(left):\r\n                nums[i] = left[j]\r\n                j += 1\r\n                i += 1\r\n            while k < len(right):\r\n                nums[i] = right[k]\r\n                k += 1\r\n                i += 1\r\n\r\n        def mergeSort(arr, l, r):\r\n            if l == r:\r\n                return arr\r\n            m = (l + r) // 2\r\n            mergeSort(arr, l, m)\r\n            mergeSort(arr, m + 1, r)\r\n            merge(arr, l, m, r)\r\n            return arr\r\n        \r\n        return mergeSort(nums, 0, len(nums) - 1)",
