      {
        "rung": 2,
        "text": "We can store the prefix maximum in an array by iterating from left to right and the suffix maximum in another array by iterating from right to left. For example, in [1, 5, 2, 3, 4], for the element 3, the prefix maximum is 5, and the suffix maximum is 4. Once these arrays are built, we can iterate through the array with index i and calculate the total water trapped at each position using the formula: min(prefix[i], suffix[i]) - height[i]."
      }
