        "rung": 2,
        "text": "We can use a stack to maintain the times of the fleets. As we iterate through the array (sorted in descending order of positions), we compute the time for each car to reach the target and check if it can form a fleet with the car ahead. If the current car's time is less than or equal to the top of the stack, it joins the same fleet. Otherwise, it forms a new fleet, and we push its time onto the stack. The length of the stack at the end represents the total number of fleets formed."
