        "text": "The core pattern is **Linked List**. To achieve O(1) operations, we need fast access to a key's current node and to the least recently used node inside each frequency group. We use a hash map from frequency to a doubly linked list of cache nodes, and a separate key-to-node map for direct access. Each linked list maintains recency order within one frequency bucket, so the head is the eviction candidate for ties. We also track the current minimum frequency to quickly find which list to evict from."
