        "text": "The core pattern is **Heap / Priority Queue**. Instead of using a min-heap for capital, we can simply sort the projects by their capital requirements upfront. A pointer then tracks which projects have become affordable. As capital grows, we advance this pointer and push newly affordable project profits into a max-heap. This avoids repeated heap operations on the capital side and is often faster in practice due to better cache performance from the sorted array traversal."
