        "text": "We can use Hierholzer's algorithm, a modified DFS approach. Instead of appending the node to the result list immediately, we first visit all its neighbors. This results in a post-order traversal. After completing all the DFS calls, we reverse the path to obtain the final path, which is also called Euler's path."
