        "rung": 1,
        "text": "The core pattern is **1-D Dynamic Programming**. Notice that to compute T(n), we only need the three most recent values: T(n-1), T(n-2), and T(n-3). We do not need to store the entire history. By keeping just three variables (or a small fixed-size array), we can reduce space complexity from O(n) to O(1).\n\nA clever trick uses an array of size 3 and the modulo operator. At iteration i, we store the new value at index i % 3, which naturally overwrites the oldest value we no longer need."
