    "hints": [
      {
        "rung": 0,
        "text": "Since each state only depends on the next three states (`dp[i+1]`, `dp[i+2]`, `dp[i+3]`), we can reduce space from `O(n)` to `O(1)` by using a rolling array of size `4`."
      },
      {
        "rung": 1,
        "text": "The core pattern is **1-D Dynamic Programming**. Since each state only depends on the next three states (`dp[i+1]`, `dp[i+2]`, `dp[i+3]`), we can reduce space from `O(n)` to `O(1)` by using a rolling array of size `4`. We use modulo arithmetic to cycle through the array indices as we process positions from right to left."
      },
      {
        "rung": 2,
        "text": "Turn the idea into these steps:\n\n1. Create a small DP array `dp[4]` initialized to `0`.\n2. Iterate from `i = n-1` down to `0`.\n3. For each `i`, set `dp[i % 4] = negative infinity`. Try taking `1`, `2`, or `3` stones, accumulating the total and computing `dp[i % 4] = max(dp[i % 4], total - dp[(j + 1) % 4])`.\n4. The value `dp[0]` represents Alice's advantage. Return \"Alice\" if positive, \"Bob\" if negative, \"Tie\" if zero."
      }
    ],
    "walkthrough": [
      "Since each state only depends on the next three states (`dp[i+1]`, `dp[i+2]`, `dp[i+3]`), we can reduce space from `O(n)` to `O(1)` by using a rolling array of size `4`.",
      "The core pattern is **1-D Dynamic Programming**. Since each state only depends on the next three states (`dp[i+1]`, `dp[i+2]`, `dp[i+3]`), we can reduce space from `O(n)` to `O(1)` by using a rolling array of size `4`. We use modulo arithmetic to cycle through the array indices as we process positions from right to left.",
      "Turn the idea into these steps:\n\n1. Create a small DP array `dp[4]` initialized to `0`.\n2. Iterate from `i = n-1` down to `0`.\n3. For each `i`, set `dp[i % 4] = negative infinity`. Try taking `1`, `2`, or `3` stones, accumulating the total and computing `dp[i % 4] = max(dp[i % 4], total - dp[(j + 1) % 4])`.\n4. The value `dp[0]` represents Alice's advantage. Return \"Alice\" if positive, \"Bob\" if negative, \"Tie\" if zero."
    ],
    "solution": "class Solution:\r\n    def stoneGameIII(self, stoneValue: List[int]) -> str:\r\n        n = len(stoneValue)\r\n        dp = [0] * 4\r\n\r\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\r\n            total = 0\r\n            dp[i % 4] = float(\"-inf\")\r\n            for j in range(i, min(i + 3, n)):\r\n                total += stoneValue[j]\r\n                dp[i % 4] = max(dp[i % 4], total - dp[(j + 1) % 4])\r\n\r\n        if dp[0] == 0:\r\n            return \"Tie\"\r\n        return \"Alice\" if dp[0] > 0 else \"Bob\"",
