        "text": "The core pattern is **Math & Geometry**. The problem asks us to insert a new node between every pair of adjacent nodes, where the new node's value is the GCD of its neighbors. We traverse the list and for each pair of consecutive nodes, compute their `gcd` and create a new node with that value.\nThe Euclidean algorithm efficiently computes the `gcd`: repeatedly replace the larger number with the remainder of dividing the two numbers until one becomes zero. The other number is the `gcd`.\nSince we're inserting nodes as we traverse, we need to be careful to advance the pointer past the newly inserted node to avoid processing it again."
